A summary table of the min, max, and avg values of all the sampler parameters is also included automatically in shinyStan under the "Diagnose" tab. And it's probably much quicker to just  do launch_shinystan(stanfit) than try to figure out how to use get_sampler_params and then deal with the list object it gives you. In fact the entire motivation for making shinyStan was so I would never have to type 'get_sampler_params' ever again. But now I've gone and done it twice in one message.

