From u3f22b207863d2049 at groups.google.com  Thu Mar  5 11:51:44 2015
From: u3f22b207863d2049 at groups.google.com (Luc Coffeng)
Date: Thu, 05 Mar 2015 11:51:44 +0000
Subject: Re: [stan-users] How would you parametrize a markov chain model and its hierarchical extension?
Message-ID: <pIEJOTEtbAU.w45LWMLKiloJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <pIEJOTEtbAU.kzTKpN2rgvwJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
References: <pIEJOTEtbAU.KZkK0r9qh3IJ@stan-users.groups.google.com> <pIEJOTEtbAU.kzTKpN2rgvwJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-users/c/pIEJOTEtbAU/m/w45LWMLKiloJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

If you define transition matrix M per individual (M_i) and use M_i for all chains of states for a given individual, you can use a dirichlet hyperprior for columns of transition probabilities in your transition matrix M_i. However, this would only pool information for each column separately, and not account for possible correlation between column within a given matrix M_i. I don't know whether there are priors for whole transition matrices - perhaps this is something you can find literature.

