Hi!
I'm doing a comparison between different software that perform Bayesian estimation (WinBUGS, Stan, etc). I chose the population ODE model described in this presentation: http://www.bayes-pharma.org/bayes2012docs/Day2_Afternoon/9_Bays2012_Foteini_Strimenopoulou.pdf. The model is a  two compartment population PK model with linear and non linear elimination. I simulated the data with Simulx, in particular there are 6 groups of 3 individuals, each group take different doses; the administration is an infusion of 1 hour. The model I wrote in Stan compiles, but it is extremely slower than WinBUGS; I was wondering if you could have a look at my code to see if there is the possibility to speed up the sampling procedure.
Please find attached the .stan model, the R code and the simulated data I used for the estimation.
