Hi Rob,

Sure please find attached the updated version of the data set dat. Also, I made a small change in the model(see the red part):

// likelihood
  for(ii in 1:Ns){
    i <- dat[ii,1]; // animal id
    d <- dat[ii,2]; // find the group
    j <- dat[ii,3]; // finds what attribute (I changed this)
    W[i] ~ normal(X[i],sigu);
    X[i] ~ normal(al0d[d]+Zid[i]*al3d[d], signu[d]); // measurement error part
    eta[i] ~ normal(0,1);
    bijd[i,j] ~ multi_normal(mu0,lamb[j]);
    Y[ii] ~ multi_normal(rep_vector(X[i] * kap1jd[j,d] + eta[i] * bet2jd[j,d] + kap2jd[j,d] * Zid[i],tm) +  Qj * Cjd[j,d] + Qj*bijd[i,j], sigj[j]*eyetm);
  }

Thanks.

